source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:49d483cb4322cacb5aebcaf0fe84ad937def3c38424283fe709007269396bf4e","file":"preprints/A-Smooth-Metric-with-No-Local-Isometric-Immersion-into-Three-Space-September-24-2026/build/main.tex","line":70,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"5de6e36c11bf0b0549a1828e4445471e14dbdb06e947d7199dd0c6cf4f4776e8","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-Smooth-Metric-with-No-Local-Isometric-Immersion-into-Three-Space-September-24-2026/build/main.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:49d483cb4322cacb5aebcaf0fe84ad937def3c38424283fe709007269396bf4e","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-Smooth-Metric-with-No-Local-Isometric-Immersion-into-Three-Space-September-24-2026/build/main.tex#L70"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"There is a \\(C^\\infty\\) positive definite Riemannian metric \\(g\\) on\n\\((-1,1)^2\\) such that no open neighborhood \\(U\\) of the origin admits a\n\\(C^\\infty\\) isometric immersion\n\\[\nF:(U,g)\\longrightarrow\\R^3.\n\\]\nIn particular, no such neighborhood admits a smooth isometric embedding."}
